      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-07T23:26:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we execute the TODO at the top of this file, this can probably simply be replaced with NetworkAgentWrapper, and the entire file becomes unnecessary.\n\nThis would make the test more realistic, but it would also not isolate the tethering code nearly as much, so I\u0027m not too sure it\u0027s even a good idea in the first place.\n\nI guess keeping the TODO at the top of the file is probably still the best tradeoff until we need to instrument more here, which likely will see the code converge",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 226,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 226,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "564d32da3561f57d5431945116fbb5555729ebfa",
